-- title:
--   Uniqueness of a good point reading a given place
-- statement:
--   Setting and ambient fields. Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`: $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Three function fields occur. First, $\bar F_{M'}:=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions at level $M'$). Second, $\bar F_H:=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $\mathbb Q$-rational $X_H$ function field at level $q^2M'$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Third, over $\kappa$: $\mathcal C:=$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, generated over $\kappa$ by the Laurent series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $M'$, and $\mathcal X:=$ `xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\bar F_{M'}\subseteq\bar F_H$. Here `Place K F` means a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ and with principal ideals, with `ord`, `evalAt` and `IsRational` (surjectivity of $K\to$ residue field) as in the project's definitions.
--
--   Supersingular places. `W` is a finite set of places of $\mathcal C$ over $\kappa$ and `hW` says that its members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w$-value of `jGeomGen κ M'` in `ssJSet q κ`, the set of those $j\in\kappa$ for which every elliptic curve over $\kappa$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   Constant reduction. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction A ↥(modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_{M'}$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $\mathcal C$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a place map to places of $\mathcal C$, compatibility with $A$ on constants, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a scalar $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral and nonzero residue, preservation of degrees and of divisors (`deg_placeMap`, `mapDomain_placeMap`). The hypothesis `hR₀` says that whenever $y$ is a Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Igusa family. A primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` is given, together with families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)\to$ {valuation subrings of $\bar F_H$} and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}:W\to$ {valuation subrings of $\bar F_H$}. The hypotheses on $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ are: `hIg_inf`, that $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (with $\infty=$ `lineInfty q` the point $[1:0]$) holds exactly when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y=x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent series; `hIg`, that each line $\ell$ is of the form `redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ taking preimages under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   Supersingular family. The hypotheses on $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ having no pole at any place of $\bar F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j_q$ has no pole, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in $\bar F_H$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is its own preimage under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   Regular prolongation. $R$ is a `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC κ (q^2*M') (levelH q M'))`, that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F_H$ with a surjective residue map onto $\mathcal X$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and with the scaling property; `hR` identifies $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` says that $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when its image in $\bar F_H$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   Local constants and layers. Further data: an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, with algebraically closed residue field (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`), together with `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Also a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Quantification in the conclusion. With $\bar F_H$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is universally quantified over an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\bar F_H/k_0$ satisfying: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F_H$ is all of $\bar F_H$; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar F_H$ with all $a_i$ in the compositum of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_ia_i=0$ then all $a_i=0$; and $F_0$ contains every element of $\bar F_H$ whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, that is, has rational coefficients.
--
--   Put $T_1$ for the compositum, inside $\bar F_H$, of the image of $K_1$ and of $F_0$. The quantification continues over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\bar F_H$; over a nonzero element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $\bar F_H$ is the inclusion of the element of $\bar F_{M'}$ given by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$; and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of $\mathcal X$ over $\kappa$ for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j:\mathcal C\to\mathcal X$ such that (a) for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in $\bar F_H$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is $j$ applied to its $R_0$-residue, and (b) $Q\in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds exactly when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ in the valuation ring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation ring of $Q$, for all $g\in\mathcal C$.
--
--   The model and the predicates. Let $\mathfrak X_1:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with structural morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` and `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$. The statement introduces, for a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$:
--
--   `InStalk x f`: for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` whose image under `ιFin` is $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgInf` over $x$ with `chartAlgInf` in place of `chartAlgFin`.
--
--   `InMax x f`: the same, with the extra requirement $g\in y$ in both clauses.
--
--   `Centred P x`, for $P$ a place of $\bar F_H$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: $P$ is rational, and for every $f\in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` the image of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $P$, its value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ lies in $A$, and that value has $A$-valuation $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`.
--
--   `GoodPt x`: the image of $x$ under `toBase` is the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_1$; $x$ admits no proper specialisation, i.e. $x\rightsquigarrow y$ forces $y=x$; for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every $b$ in `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\bar F_H$ is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y$, and the same with `chartAlgInf`; and for every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   `Reads x Q`, for $Q$ a place of $\mathcal X$ over $\kappa$: for every $f\in T_1$ with `InStalk x f`, the image of $f$ in $\bar F_H$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $Q$, and that residue is a nonunit of the valuation ring of $Q$ if and only if `InMax x f`.
--
--   `OffBranch x`: for every line $\ell\ne\infty$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and every prime $y$ of `chartAlgFin` over $x$ there is $b$ in `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\bar F_H$ is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ with $b\notin y$, and the same with `chartAlgInf`.
--
--   Conclusion. For all points $x,x'$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt`, and for every place $Q$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\kappa$ such that both `Reads x Q` and `Reads x' Q` hold, one has $x=x'$. The conclusion mentions only `GoodPt` and `Reads`; the predicates `Centred` and `OffBranch` and the finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ with its compatibility hypothesis belong to the frame in which the statement is placed and serve to keep it aligned with the companion statements about the same model.
--
--   This is the separatedness half of the analysis of the two-chart integral model of the $X_H$-curve at level $q^2M'$ over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$: a closed point of the special fibre lying on the $\infty$-Igusa component and away from supersingular $j$-invariants is determined by the place of the residual $X_H$ function field that it reads. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), in the construction of the semistable reduction data attached to the Igusa components at $q$ that underlies the level-lowering step.
